   "subject": "Re: Question regarding DIF exercise 2 syntax from Zurich workshop",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Daniel,<div><br></div><div>I believe the &#39;free_varcov&#39; keyword was replaced sometime back, and now only &#39;free_var&#39; should be used to free the latent variances in the focal group(s). Sorry for the confusion.</div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Fri, Jun 22, 2018 at 5:17 PM Daniel McKelvey &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">daniel.k...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Phil,<div><br></div><div>I am conducting some DIF analyses and I was following the syntax from <a href=\"https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/wiki\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/wiki&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473504574000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3uDtsX9MbOhlOrB3RRXk1_\">Zurich exercise 2 </a>in order to do so when I noticed a piece of syntax that I wasn&#39;t sure about. When I got to here:<br><ol style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;margin-bottom:10px;margin-top:0px\" start=\"4\"><li style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">The items appear to be behaving differently for each group in the completely independent model. This is an indication that there are either population difference between the groups, the items are showing DIF, or both.</li>\r\n</ol><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal\">\r\n</span><ul style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;margin-bottom:10px;margin-top:0px\">\r\n<li style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">First, we will adjust the data to account for group differences. Fit a less constrained versions of the ‘completely equal’ model, where the mean and variance for the second group are freely estimated, but keep the intercepts and slopes equal across groups (Hint: See the <code style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.04);border-radius:4px;box-sizing:border-box;font-size:12.6px;padding:2px 4px;white-space:pre-wrap\">invariance = &#39;&#39;</code> argument in <code style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.04);border-radius:4px;box-sizing:border-box;font-size:12.6px;padding:2px 4px;white-space:pre-wrap\">?multipleGroup</code>). Use a likelihood ratio test to determine if the model fits significantly better after freely estimating these parameters.</li>\r\n</ul><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal\">\r\n</span><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;line-height:18.57px;margin-bottom:10px;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word\"><code style=\"background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px;box-sizing:border-box;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mod.freegroup</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">multipleGroup</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group</span>, \r\n                      <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">invariance</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;intercepts&#39;</span>,<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;slopes&#39;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;free_means&#39;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;free_varcov&#39;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I wasn&#39;t sure whether it was supposed to be the &#39;free_varcov&#39; argument that was passed, as in the provided syntax, or whether it was supposed to be the &#39;free_var&#39; argument as seems to be implied by the bullet point.</div><div><br></div><div>A little later, the exercise says:</div><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;line-height:18.57px;margin-bottom:10px;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word\"><code style=\"background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px;box-sizing:border-box;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#group with training appears to have a higher group mean, but with more variance</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">coef</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mod.freegroup</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">GroupPars</span></code></pre><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal\">\r\n</span><pre style=\"border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;line-height:18.57px;margin-bottom:10px;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word\"><code style=\"background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px;box-sizing:border-box;white-space:pre-wrap\">##     MEAN_1 COV_11 </code></pre><div><span style=\"background-color:transparent;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">## par  0.879      1</span> </div><div><br></div><div>and later when the DIF corrected model is created it uses this syntax:<br><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">model</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">mirt.model</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">&#39;Theta = 1-20\r\n                    CONSTRAINB = (1,4-18,20, a1), (1-18,20, d)&#39;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">)</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">\r\n</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">final.mod</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">multipleGroup</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">data</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">, </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">model</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">, </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">group</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">=</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">group</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">, </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">SE</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">=</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,0,115);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">TRUE</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">,\r\n                           </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">invariance</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">=</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">c</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">&#39;free_means&#39;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">, </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">&#39;free_var&#39;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">)</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\">)</span><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:transparent;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135);font-family:monospace;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div>It seems to me that the &#39;free_varcov&#39; argument was included in the solved exercise by mistake when it was supposed to be the &#39;free_var&#39; argument? I could be wrong on this, but I wanted to double check before I changed my syntax around.<div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance!</div><div>Daniel</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
